DP  - 2025 Aug 7
TI  - Transfer Learning Enhances Neurological Outcome Prediction for Out-of-Hospital 
      Cardiac Arrest: Validation Across Diverse Geographic Contexts.
PG  - 1962-1963
LID - 10.3233/SHTI251300 [doi]
AB  - Developing accurate risk stratification models for out-of-hospital cardiac arrest 
      (OHCA) in low-resource settings is challenging due to small sample sizes and poor 
      data quality. The Pan-Asian Resuscitation Outcomes Study (PAROS) network provides 
      a valuable OHCA registry across the Asia-Pacific region, but limited data 
      availability, such as in Vietnam, hampers robust model development. Transfer 
      learning (TL), a machine learning technique, can address these challenges by 
      adapting pre-trained models to new contexts. We used TL to adapt an OHCA 
      neurological outcome prediction model from a large Japanese cohort to Vietnam (n 
      = 243) and Singapore (n = 15,916), representing low- and high-resource settings. 
      TL significantly improved performance in Vietnam (AUROC: 0.807 vs. 0.467) and 
      modestly enhanced outcomes in Singapore, demonstrating its potential to overcome 
      data limitations and improve prediction accuracy in diverse healthcare settings.
